            <ArticleTitle>The syndrome of painful ophthalmoplegia. A case with intraorbital mass and hypervascularity.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>41-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A patient diagnosed as having Tolosa-Hunt syndrome on clinical grounds was found by arteriography to have an intraorbital mass with hypervascularity. To our knowledge, this radiologic finding has not previously been reported in either Tolosa-Hunt syndrome or in the syndrome of orbital pseudotumor, and supports the proposition that these two conditions are anatomical variants of the same pathological process.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
